//!
//! **Generated by `tools/gen_theme_egui.py`. Do not edit.**
//!
//! Everything below is a value read out of the Modrinth App's vendored CSS at
//! the commit `vendor/modrinth-app/UPSTREAM.md` pins, resolved the way a browser
//! would resolve it: comments stripped, multi-line declarations joined, `@extend`
//! chains followed, and `var()` indirection followed to a fixed point before
//! anything was written. The tool is `tools/gen_theme_egui.py`; the gate is
//! `python tools/gen_theme_egui.py --check`, which regenerates this file in memory
//! and compares it byte for byte.
//!
//! The names are the CSS custom properties in SCREAMING_SNAKE, with the `--color-`
//! prefix dropped because the field is already a colour: `--color-bg` is
//! [`Theme::BG`], `--color-raised-bg` is [`Theme::RAISED_BG`]. Every initialiser in
//! [`DARK`] and [`LIGHT`] carries the sheet, the line and the `var()` chain it came
//! through, so a stale value traces back to the line that moved.
//!
//! A token the sheet wrote as `rgb()`/a hex triple is stored with `from_rgb`. The few
//! it wrote as `rgba(..., a)` with a < 1 are stored with `from_rgba_premultiplied`, the
//! const form of the same colour (`from_rgba_unmultiplied` is not a `const fn` in
//! every egui version, and these live in `const`s); the alpha they declare is stated
//! beside each and asserted in the tests.
//!
//! | Source | What came out of it |
//! | --- | --- |
//! | `assets/styles/variables.scss` | 67 colour tokens, 6 radii, 5 gaps |
//! | `assets/styles/defaults.scss` | 3 font sizes, 3 font weights |
//! | `ui/src/styles/tailwind-utilities.css` | `--ease-out-expo`, and the popover and floating-bar transitions |
//!
//! Written against egui 0.36.1. The crate's egui source was not on the machine this
//! was generated on, so the fields `colors()` touches are assumed from the 0.31
//! renames: `Visuals::window_corner_radius`, `WidgetVisuals::corner_radius` and
//! `CornerRadius::same(u8)`. If a build says a field does not exist, that is what
